.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt PKCS12_SAFEBAG_GET0_ATTRS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm PKCS12_SAFEBAG_get0_attrs ,
.Nm PKCS12_get_attr_gen
.Nd Retrieve attributes from a PKCS#12 safeBag
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pkcs12.h
.Ft const
.Fo STACK_OF
.Fa X509_ATTRIBUTE
.Fc
 *PKCS12_SAFEBAG_get0_attrs(const PKCS12_SAFEBAG *bag);
.Ft ASN1_TYPE *
.Fo PKCS12_get_attr_gen
.Fa "const STACK_OF(X509_ATTRIBUTE) *attrs"
.Fa "int attr_nid"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr PKCS12_SAFEBAG_get0_attrs 3
retrieves the stack of
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE Ns s
from a PKCS#12 safeBag.
.Em bag
is the
.Sy PKCS12_SAFEBAG
to retrieve the attributes from.
.Pp
.Fn PKCS12_get_attr_gen
retrieves an attribute by NID from a stack of
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE Ns s.
.Fa attr_nid
is the NID of the attribute to retrieve.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Xr PKCS12_SAFEBAG_get0_attrs 3
returns the stack of
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE Ns s
from a PKCS#12 safeBag, which could be empty.
.Pp
.Fn PKCS12_get_attr_gen
returns an
.Vt ASN1_TYPE
object containing the attribute, or NULL if the attribute was either not
present or an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn PKCS12_get_attr_gen
does not allocate a new attribute.
The returned attribute is still owned by the
.Sy PKCS12_SAFEBAG
in which it resides.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr PKCS12_get_friendlyname 3 ,
.Xr PKCS12_add_friendlyname_asc 3
